  "worked_solution": "First, we must determine the temperature of the liquid when removing it from the refrigerator. Since its temperature decreased by ${17.1}^{∘}\\text{C}$ compared to its initial temperature, we must subtract the variation in temperature from the initial temperature. This gives\n\n$$\n{15.3}^{∘}\\text{C}-{17.1}^{∘}\\text{C}=-{1.8}^{∘}\\text{C}.\n$$\n\nNow, we must determine the temperature of the liquid after the $15$ minutes outside the refrigerator. Since the temperature of the liquid increased by ${6}^{∘}\\text{C}$ compared to the temperature it had when it was removed from the refrigerator, we add the variation in temperature to the temperature of the liquid when it was removed from the refrigerator. This gives\n\n$$\n-{1.8}^{∘}\\text{C}+{6}^{∘}\\text{C}={4.2}^{∘}\\text{C}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the final temperature of the liquid was ${4.2}^{∘}\\text{C}.$",
